## Project 3eeb8053-2ce1-4573-97bb-00ea871a8ad1 · Session 744e6431-cfe6-452d-9d8f-e17ee5eafcb3 (2026-04-22)

### 原始困境（Raw Input）
女儿要不要送到国际学校幼儿园读书？我在上海，其实是想送到大理那种纯自然的环境读书（充分的解放天性），但是家庭情况不允许：我自己是自由职业（每年 20-40w 的收入），太太在银行工作（20-30w 收入）； 我自己从 NYU 硕士毕业，小时候是小镇做题家，考到了复旦本科；但是在复旦非常痛苦，失去了方向 ～典型的空心病

### 锁定议题（Defined Topic）
核心问题：在上海的现实条件下，如何为女儿构建一个既能提供“解放天性”核心体验、又符合家庭财务可持续性的个性化成长方案，而非在“大理自然教育”与“国际学校”这两个抽象标签间做二选一。

你可能也在想：
· 如何将“解放天性”这一理想，解构为在上海可落地、可负担的具体日常体验（如户外时长、探索方式），并评估不同学校或家庭自身能提供多少。
· 在财务安全（根据地）与教育理想之间，家庭可承受的、具体的学费支出红线是多少，以及超出部分如何通过非学校教育模块（如利用你的时间灵活性整合城市资源）来弥补。

### 挖事实 — 案主的回答（Step 3 Facts · 身份层最高信号）
> 此段是案主在具体问题情境下的自然反应，context-density 最高，是 User Wiki 身份层的脊柱素材。

## 李小龙 Questions
Have you measured the exact weekly hours of unstructured outdoor play and exploration your daughter currently experiences in her daily routine?

What is the specific, non-negotiable monthly tuition budget you have calculated that would not compromise your family's financial stability and sense of security?

## Client's Answer
我们没有精确测量过每周具体的户外自由活动时长，但意识到目前日常安排中这部分确实不足。经过计算，我们认为每月用于教育支出的、不影响家庭财务安全感的非协商预算上限大约在8,000至10,000元人民币。


## 六祖慧能 Questions
Have you measured how many hours per week your daughter currently spends in direct, unstructured contact with natural elements (soil, water, plants, sunlight) versus structured indoor activities?

## Client's Answer
目前我女儿每周接触自然的时间很少，大约只有周末的2-3小时在公园，其余大部分是室内的早教和家庭活动。我意识到这与我期望的“解放天性”差距很大，正在思考如何在上海增加她日常与自然接触的机会。


## Kevin Kelly Questions
What is the specific monthly or annual tuition range you are considering for an "international school kindergarten" in Shanghai, and what percentage of your combined household income would that represent?

## Client's Answer
我们考虑的国际学校幼儿园学费范围大约在每月1.5万至2.5万元人民币，按年计算约18万至30万元。这大约占我们家庭年收入（40万至70万元）的30%到50%，对我们来说是一个需要谨慎权衡的财务负担。


## 毛泽东 Questions
Have you conducted a "rural investigation" of the specific international schools and local public or alternative schools in your area, comparing their daily schedules, outdoor space, and teacher-student interaction patterns to see which truly offers more "liberation of nature" in practice?

What is the precise "battlefield terrain" of your family finances—the exact monthly surplus after all fixed expenses, and what percentage of that surplus would a proposed school tuition consume?

## Client's Answer
我没有进行过如此具体的“农村调查”式实地对比，目前更多是基于网络信息和口碑的初步了解。

家庭每月固定开支后的盈余大约在1.5万至2.5万元人民币，如果选择一所典型的上海国际学校幼儿园，其学费很可能将消耗这个盈余的60%甚至全部，这会使我们的财务“根据地”变得非常脆弱。


## Paul Graham Questions
Have you calculated your family's monthly "burn rate" and runway if you commit to the full cost of an international school kindergarten in Shanghai?

What is the minimum viable "outdoor/exploration time" per week that you believe would constitute the core of "liberating her nature" for your daughter?

## Client's Answer
We have not calculated a precise burn rate, but committing to a full-cost international kindergarten in Shanghai would significantly strain our finances and drastically shorten our runway, given our variable combined income of 40-70w annually. For the core of "liberating her nature," we believe a minimum of 10-15 hours per week of dedicated, unstructured outdoor and exploration time in Shanghai's parks, riversides, and museums would be essential and achievable.


## Steve Jobs Questions
Have you mapped out the exact weekly hours and types of "liberating nature" experiences you want for your daughter, and compared that to the specific daily schedule of the international school kindergarten you're considering?

What is the maximum percentage of your combined annual income you are willing to commit to tuition, before you start building the "liberal arts" part of her education yourself with your flexible time?

## Client's Answer
No, I haven't mapped out the exact weekly hours yet, but that's the crucial next step to compare concrete schedules. We are willing to commit a maximum of 20-25% of our combined annual income to formal tuition, reserving the rest of our resources—especially my flexible time—to actively build and fund the "liberal arts" and nature experiences for her myself.

### 案主自己的反思（Client's Own Reflection）
